# Terraform Conventions

- All AWS resources are managed in Terraform; no manual console changes.
- Organise as reusable modules (`modules/`) consumed by environments
  (`environments/local`, `environments/dev`). Each module has `variables.tf`,
  `main.tf`, `outputs.tf`.
- The `local` environment targets LocalStack endpoints; `dev` targets real AWS.
- Always run `terraform fmt` and `terraform validate`; tflint and Checkov must
  pass.
- IAM policies are least privilege and resource-scoped (no `*` on resources or
  actions unless justified with a comment).
- No secrets in code or state; use SSM Parameter Store / Secrets Manager.
- Name resources with a consistent prefix and environment suffix.

```hcl
# GOOD: scoped, least-privilege statement
statement {
  actions   = ["dynamodb:PutItem", "dynamodb:UpdateItem"]
  resources = [aws_dynamodb_table.documents.arn]
}
```
